  "findings": [
    "Reducing the optimizer step from 0.04 to 0.012 exposes more distinct target-specific patterns while preserving a readable scene in this sample.",
    "The arches and organic candidates were selected for different visual structures. The cellular control still quickly creates a repeating pebble-like texture.",
    "Ten recursive model stages completed, but the subject stretches and the scene loses clarity; this method does not establish a convincing forward-travel illusion.",
    "The no-further-inference control also develops radial stretching and blur. This implicates repeated perspective capture, planar photo placement, and resampling; the streaking cannot be attributed solely to the models.",
    "Model-generated patterns remain visible in the synthesis chain beyond the resampling effects demonstrated by the control."
  ],
  "nextExperiment": "Calibrate perspective-to-panorama round-trip projection with inference disabled, then repeat the forward chain while preserving angular coordinates. Evaluate checkpoint refresh only after geometric drift is controlled.",
  "limitations": [
    "One low-resolution marmot photo, six feature targets, two strengths, and one native GPU configuration.",
    "Forward stages are discrete keyframes. Playback is a review aid, not a smooth movement implementation.",
    "No demonstration of endless coherent scene generation, full-history backtracking, or simultaneous-generation rendering performance.",
    "No authored wave, refraction, chromatic dispersion, relief, or camera-translation effects were used.",
    "Generated images remain local in ignored test-results; source tools and measurements are versioned."
